+---
+id: dl-004-bulk-import-is-a-line-parser-over-list.add
+type: decision-log
+title: "Bulk import is a line parser over list.add"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## Context
+
+Teams move to Tidy Tasks from spreadsheets and need to load many tasks from text.
+
+## Decision
+
+`importTasks` only parses lines and delegates to `list.add`, so validation, duplicates and ids follow
+the list's rules (dl-003). Line numbers count from 1 and include blank lines, which are skipped. Lines are
+split on `\n`, `\r\n` or `\r`. A line with more than three `;`-fields is rejected rather than guessing
+where a title ends. Priority is trimmed but case-sensitive. A title repeated in the text is rejected as a
+duplicate. A bad line never stops the others, and the function never throws.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The report is a plain object, not a `Result`, as the import as a whole cannot fail. A `;` cannot appear in a title.
